1
00:00:05,836 --> 00:00:07,282
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,309 --> 00:00:08,799
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:10,512 --> 00:00:12,685
(Episode 26)

4
00:00:13,052 --> 00:00:17,226
Smells so sweet. I can finally breathe.

5
00:00:42,882 --> 00:00:46,406
Because of you,
I haven't slept or showered.

6
00:00:46,759 --> 00:00:48,926
Do you know how many days I've been
staking you out from my car?

7
00:00:49,569 --> 00:00:53,271
Get lost. I can't stand the sight of you,
so get lost.

8
00:00:57,046 --> 00:00:58,682
Want to get hit, or just leave?

9
00:00:59,939 --> 00:01:02,049
Help me!

10
00:01:07,077 --> 00:01:08,703
Hey, let go.

11
00:01:08,728 --> 00:01:11,341
Help me!

12
00:01:12,889 --> 00:01:14,742
Let go!

13
00:01:18,978 --> 00:01:21,017
Sir, help me!

14
00:01:22,104 --> 00:01:24,009
She's my wife.
She ran off with another man.

15
00:01:24,409 --> 00:01:27,616
Honey, please come to your senses!

16
00:01:27,842 --> 00:01:30,304
Our baby's crying for you right now.

17
00:01:30,668 --> 00:01:32,003
He's lying.

18
00:01:32,342 --> 00:01:34,441
You should think of your child.

19
00:01:34,536 --> 00:01:37,164
Please come to your senses, honey!

20
00:01:38,856 --> 00:01:42,676
Get in. Let's go home now.

21
00:01:43,702 --> 00:01:44,729
Gyu Yeong?

22
00:01:45,161 --> 00:01:47,369
- Han Gyu Seo!
- Gyu Yeong!

23
00:01:49,368 --> 00:01:52,566
- Who are you?
- What?

24
00:01:52,591 --> 00:01:55,712
- Gyu Yeong!
- Gyu Yeong!

25
00:01:58,073 --> 00:01:59,709
Han Gyu Yeong!

26
00:02:00,732 --> 00:02:01,956
Where do you think you're going?

27
00:02:02,001 --> 00:02:04,829
Let go! Let go, you jerk.

28
00:02:05,428 --> 00:02:07,791
And who are you, you jerk?

29
00:02:08,689 --> 00:02:10,149
You think I'm a pushover?

30
00:02:11,398 --> 00:02:15,048
This looks expensive. Did someone drop it?

31
00:02:18,049 --> 00:02:20,399
Gyu Yeong. What's wrong with you?

32
00:02:20,573 --> 00:02:23,806
Hey! Gyu Yeong!

33
00:02:23,831 --> 00:02:25,799
It's me! Heung Sik!

34
00:02:40,016 --> 00:02:44,023
Heung Sik!

35
00:02:47,466 --> 00:02:51,333
Okay. Did something happen?

36
00:03:00,462 --> 00:03:03,776
Hey, Gyu Seo!

37
00:03:03,801 --> 00:03:08,391
- It hurts.
- Hey, what happened to you?

38
00:03:08,881 --> 00:03:11,218
And what's all this?

39
00:03:11,249 --> 00:03:13,545
Did that psycho Seong Uk do this?

40
00:03:13,909 --> 00:03:16,429
I was on my way to deliver rice cakes
for Gyu O's store opening...

41
00:03:17,201 --> 00:03:18,841
Who is that jerk?

42
00:03:19,249 --> 00:03:21,413
Why is he trying to kidnap Gyu Yeong?

43
00:03:21,529 --> 00:03:23,780
And why on earth is Gyu Yeong here?

44
00:03:23,862 --> 00:03:28,003
He's supposedly Gyu Yeong's husband.
It's a long story.

45
00:03:28,196 --> 00:03:30,276
Let's call an ambulance first.

46
00:03:36,829 --> 00:03:42,074
You're not even in your right mind.
How could you wander off like that?

47
00:03:43,149 --> 00:03:46,830
I dozed off for a second watching TV,

48
00:03:46,862 --> 00:03:50,450
and you slipped out just like that.

49
00:03:52,816 --> 00:03:57,047
No.

50
00:03:57,072 --> 00:03:59,687
I'm not scolding you.

51
00:04:00,076 --> 00:04:05,617
It breaks my heart to see you like this.

52
00:04:05,642 --> 00:04:07,579
It makes my blood boil too.

53
00:04:08,036 --> 00:04:10,583
Just wait till I catch whoever did this.

54
00:04:10,608 --> 00:04:15,847
I'll rip his guts out
and jump rope with them!

55
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:18,234
Grandma...

56
00:04:21,981 --> 00:04:26,721
Still, I'm so glad it wasn't worse.

57
00:04:27,068 --> 00:04:32,701
Heung Sik called earlier and said
someone helped you?

58
00:04:33,575 --> 00:04:40,273
People say the world's a cold place,
but there are still good people out there.

59
00:04:42,242 --> 00:04:45,243
I guess that's what makes
life worth living.

60
00:04:46,863 --> 00:04:52,429
Should we put honey on some rice cakes
and have a tasty snack?

61
00:04:52,982 --> 00:04:56,738
Let's go.

62
00:04:57,208 --> 00:04:59,067
Can you bring them to me, Grandma?

63
00:04:59,209 --> 00:05:04,166
You want me to? You don't feel like going?
All right.

64
00:05:12,396 --> 00:05:14,602
(Emergency Room)

65
00:05:16,058 --> 00:05:18,015
You punk.

66
00:05:20,462 --> 00:05:22,682
Still, it's a huge relief it wasn't worse.

67
00:05:22,782 --> 00:05:26,495
No organ damage, and no broken bones.

68
00:05:26,636 --> 00:05:31,478
So you're saying Gyu Yeong
got tricked into marriage?

69
00:05:35,423 --> 00:05:37,957
Gyu Yeong lied about
who her father was too,

70
00:05:38,132 --> 00:05:42,025
and posed as a conglomerate heiress,
so she's just as guilty,

71
00:05:42,084 --> 00:05:44,358
which is why she can't go to the police.

72
00:05:46,268 --> 00:05:51,099
Compared to those lowlife in-laws,
Gyu Yeong's con is a drop in the bucket.

73
00:05:52,455 --> 00:05:54,644
When will Gyu Yeong ever grow up?

74
00:05:55,529 --> 00:05:57,392
When she's old and senile?

75
00:05:57,949 --> 00:06:00,058
Just think, "Serves her right." Okay?

76
00:06:00,109 --> 00:06:04,242
She bullied you twins so much.

77
00:06:04,568 --> 00:06:07,696
Think of it as her punishment
for being nasty to you.

78
00:06:08,162 --> 00:06:12,204
That way, you'll stress less
and heal faster too.

79
00:06:12,635 --> 00:06:14,801
Yes. That's the plan.

80
00:06:15,488 --> 00:06:19,004
"Serves her right. So satisfying.
Dopamine rush."

81
00:06:19,471 --> 00:06:21,038
That's what I'll think.

82
00:06:21,809 --> 00:06:25,173
Easier said than done. Can you really?

83
00:06:25,709 --> 00:06:31,239
Not when you charged in to save
your sister, knowing you could die.

84
00:06:34,315 --> 00:06:36,579
That's why blood is thicker than water.

85
00:06:36,829 --> 00:06:40,037
No, it's not.
We decided to cut ties with each other.

86
00:06:40,087 --> 00:06:43,573
Right. You're not okay, actually.

87
00:06:43,976 --> 00:06:47,167
They said your right eardrum
might be ruptured.

88
00:06:47,982 --> 00:06:52,062
They told me you should see an ENT
first thing tomorrow for a full checkup.

89
00:06:52,349 --> 00:06:53,844
I'll go with you tomorrow.

90
00:06:56,182 --> 00:06:57,601
Am I a kid?

91
00:06:58,488 --> 00:07:01,735
I can go to the hospital by myself,
so don't worry too much.

92
00:07:04,476 --> 00:07:08,763
I'm fine now. Do I have to finish this IV
before I can go home?

93
00:07:13,744 --> 00:07:15,938
Han Gyu Yeong?

94
00:07:16,102 --> 00:07:20,642
Yes. She's Gyu Rim's sister.

95
00:07:20,667 --> 00:07:23,772
What do we do?

96
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:30,302
But why would someone that smart
end up soft in the head at your house?

97
00:07:51,295 --> 00:07:54,227
Why'd you flick my forehead
all of a sudden...

98
00:07:54,656 --> 00:07:58,635
That's exactly how Heung Sik flicked her.

99
00:07:59,263 --> 00:08:00,610
That vixen...

100
00:08:01,535 --> 00:08:07,847
Gyu Yeong was being so snarky and annoying
that he flicked her forehead as a joke,

101
00:08:07,968 --> 00:08:10,968
but she suddenly passed out.

102
00:08:11,156 --> 00:08:16,171
She came to a little later, but she'd
gone completely soft in the head.

103
00:08:16,196 --> 00:08:18,777
And she forgot everything.

104
00:08:18,869 --> 00:08:20,875
That's ridiculous.

105
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:24,265
Can getting flicked once on the forehead
cause memory loss and make someone dumb?

106
00:08:24,402 --> 00:08:27,473
Is your son's hand
made of iron or something?

107
00:08:27,498 --> 00:08:29,624
Might as well be.

108
00:08:30,156 --> 00:08:36,538
One punch, six teeth.
That's one insane fist of his.

109
00:08:36,809 --> 00:08:41,013
I lost an entire commercial building
paying for that.

110
00:08:41,529 --> 00:08:43,142
Anyway.

111
00:08:44,235 --> 00:08:48,745
Since Heung Sik is the one
who did that to Gyu Yeong,

112
00:08:48,931 --> 00:08:53,999
we couldn't tell her family.
I've been hiding her at my house.

113
00:08:55,032 --> 00:08:58,016
So it's perfect that you're a lawyer.

114
00:09:00,123 --> 00:09:06,330
Hometown boy, please help me out a little.

115
00:09:07,229 --> 00:09:10,430
I'll take my punishment for what I did,

116
00:09:10,769 --> 00:09:14,009
but please, help Gyu Yeong
get her memory back.

117
00:09:14,762 --> 00:09:18,186
Well, I'm not a doctor...

118
00:09:18,223 --> 00:09:22,008
A lawyer like you must know
a doctor or two.

119
00:09:22,033 --> 00:09:23,995
Doctors and lawyers stick together, right?

120
00:09:27,522 --> 00:09:31,628
- I think I can help.
- What? How?

121
00:09:32,342 --> 00:09:35,765
I'm a psychiatrist.
Memory loss is my specialty.

122
00:09:38,015 --> 00:09:40,665
Is that true?

123
00:09:40,795 --> 00:09:43,529
You came to the right person.
I'll take care of it.

124
00:09:44,036 --> 00:09:47,064
Could I meet the patient first?

125
00:09:47,089 --> 00:09:52,137
Of course. When would be good?

126
00:09:56,366 --> 00:09:57,677
(So now we'll stop at "one-two, hook.")

127
00:09:57,702 --> 00:10:02,683
One, two. One.

128
00:10:11,141 --> 00:10:13,575
Hello, Secretary Jeong.
Did you find anything?

129
00:10:14,889 --> 00:10:18,406
Just something simple,
like self-defense...

130
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:20,491
What do you mean, "all of a sudden?"

131
00:10:20,516 --> 00:10:22,506
- It's good exercise and all...
- Dad!

132
00:10:23,782 --> 00:10:25,566
I'll call you back.

133
00:10:30,596 --> 00:10:32,887
- So you're going to fight for real now?
- What?

134
00:10:32,912 --> 00:10:34,712
What, you're going to beat them all up
with your fists?

135
00:10:37,429 --> 00:10:40,536
Why are you acting like this too, Dad?

136
00:10:40,635 --> 00:10:43,382
You used to flinch
at the mere mention of violence.

137
00:10:45,959 --> 00:10:52,231
Out of nowhere, those people are dragging
a perfectly good family into the gutter.

138
00:10:52,575 --> 00:10:57,763
Why do you keep talking like that?
What do you mean, "those people?"

139
00:10:58,235 --> 00:11:00,501
Those kids are practically family to us.

140
00:11:00,769 --> 00:11:05,862
If you're Ko Yun Hui's daughter,
Han Gyu Yeong is your sister too.

141
00:11:05,888 --> 00:11:08,903
This is driving me crazy.

142
00:11:11,336 --> 00:11:13,340
Does just throwing people together
make them a family?

143
00:11:13,476 --> 00:11:15,046
Does forcing it all to fit make a family?

144
00:11:15,715 --> 00:11:19,271
So Han Gyu Rim and I are sisters
in a love triangle over the same man?

145
00:11:19,296 --> 00:11:21,716
- That's why they called us a soap opera.
- Jang Seo Hyeon!

146
00:11:24,466 --> 00:11:26,096
No, let's stop.

147
00:11:29,669 --> 00:11:32,902
Seo Hyeon, do you remember?

148
00:11:33,416 --> 00:11:35,430
When you had appendix surgery.

149
00:11:37,448 --> 00:11:42,422
While you were in the hospital,
Gyu Rim called your mom after ten years.

150
00:11:43,149 --> 00:11:45,729
She said she really needed her mom
and asked her to come just once.

151
00:11:46,976 --> 00:11:51,016
But your mom didn't go.
She said she had to stay by your bedside.

152
00:11:53,749 --> 00:11:57,917
After that, Gyu Rim must've changed
her number, and we lost touch.

153
00:12:00,175 --> 00:12:04,364
Anyway, it's always bothered me.

154
00:12:05,542 --> 00:12:08,049
I feel like I owe Gyu Rim big time.

155
00:12:10,762 --> 00:12:12,113
Just...

156
00:12:14,147 --> 00:12:15,880
I just want you to know.

157
00:12:36,829 --> 00:12:43,445
Gyu O. What were you trying to say?

158
00:12:43,470 --> 00:12:44,545
(Gyu O)

159
00:12:44,570 --> 00:12:46,069
(This message was unsent.)

160
00:12:47,656 --> 00:12:50,451
What did you want to tell me?

161
00:12:51,926 --> 00:12:55,759
(Congrats on Your Store Opening,
Han Gyu O)

162
00:12:57,728 --> 00:12:59,268
Congratulations, Han Gyu O.

163
00:12:59,322 --> 00:13:02,029
Hope your store blows up
and you die counting your money!

164
00:13:05,129 --> 00:13:07,358
I'm so sorry I couldn't make it
to the opening.

165
00:13:08,182 --> 00:13:11,691
What with Gyeol, my future father-in-law,
and sisters-in-law being there,

166
00:13:11,825 --> 00:13:15,485
it didn't seem like the right day
to drop the bomb that I'm your girlfriend.

167
00:13:15,655 --> 00:13:18,961
Good call. Today was total chaos.

168
00:13:19,037 --> 00:13:21,116
Even if you'd come,
I wouldn't have had time for you.

169
00:13:21,182 --> 00:13:24,466
What should I give you?
As an opening gift.

170
00:13:27,089 --> 00:13:29,327
A dance? A song?

171
00:13:30,429 --> 00:13:31,867
Let's get married, Gyu O.

172
00:13:33,294 --> 00:13:35,034
Let's get married today.

173
00:13:35,348 --> 00:13:39,298
There's a cathedral and a church
near my place,

174
00:13:39,465 --> 00:13:41,472
and a temple if we walk 30 minutes.

175
00:13:42,741 --> 00:13:45,074
Or...

176
00:13:52,196 --> 00:13:55,486
This is a photo of my late grandparents.

177
00:13:55,806 --> 00:13:57,600
We can make our vows in front of it.

178
00:14:05,216 --> 00:14:06,620
This is cold water.

179
00:14:07,207 --> 00:14:09,887
Didn't people use to get married
with just a bowl of cold water?

180
00:14:11,167 --> 00:14:12,721
Why are you being like this
all of a sudden?

181
00:14:13,635 --> 00:14:15,195
You don't want to marry me?

182
00:14:17,622 --> 00:14:19,399
We should get our parents' blessing first.

183
00:14:19,436 --> 00:14:21,596
Our families haven't even met yet.

184
00:14:21,915 --> 00:14:23,482
We're not kids.

185
00:14:24,136 --> 00:14:27,136
We're old enough to get married
without our parents' consent.

186
00:14:27,836 --> 00:14:29,428
Still, this isn't right.

187
00:14:29,876 --> 00:14:35,632
Not until I make more money
and I'm on your level.

188
00:14:36,132 --> 00:14:38,552
Not until I can hold
my head up around you.

189
00:14:39,056 --> 00:14:43,471
My dad's business failed. He rents
a small apartment out of town,

190
00:14:43,545 --> 00:14:47,918
and my brother was in an accident.
He's disabled and uses a wheelchair now.

191
00:14:49,929 --> 00:14:53,709
And the shock seems to have given my dad
a touch of dementia.

192
00:14:54,409 --> 00:14:56,302
So we've got some debt to pay off too.

193
00:14:58,136 --> 00:15:01,630
So every month, two-thirds of my salary
goes to my family.

194
00:15:04,123 --> 00:15:08,256
Up until three months ago, we were one
of the richest families in town,

195
00:15:08,816 --> 00:15:12,429
but we went completely broke
at the speed of light.

196
00:15:15,615 --> 00:15:19,399
From now on, I'll be pinching every penny
with the other third of my salary,

197
00:15:19,526 --> 00:15:21,373
and I might nag you a lot.

198
00:15:22,356 --> 00:15:26,766
For a while, forget about a nice house,
nice clothes,

199
00:15:27,333 --> 00:15:29,040
and good food.

200
00:15:31,289 --> 00:15:36,341
Normally, with family problems like these,
marriage would be out of the question,

201
00:15:36,621 --> 00:15:39,628
but I don't care. I have to get married.

202
00:15:41,322 --> 00:15:46,483
I want to give up a hundred times a day,
so I need you right by my side.

203
00:15:51,582 --> 00:15:55,262
I thought you were just a spoiled brat,
but you're a good person.

204
00:15:55,435 --> 00:15:58,577
You're not running away,
and you even want to pay off their debt.

205
00:15:59,875 --> 00:16:04,352
If my parents pass away,
I'll take care of my brother too.

206
00:16:04,483 --> 00:16:06,989
Are you crazy?
How would you take care of him?

207
00:16:07,014 --> 00:16:09,136
- A stiff breeze would knock you over.
- What?

208
00:16:09,542 --> 00:16:13,433
I'll look after your brother, man to man.
I'll even help him bathe.

209
00:16:14,442 --> 00:16:15,830
Han Gyu O...

210
00:16:23,849 --> 00:16:27,822
Kwon Hui Na and I
are getting married today.

211
00:16:28,029 --> 00:16:30,833
Please be our witnesses, Grandpa, Grandma.

212
00:16:31,829 --> 00:16:34,089
You really want to get married right now?

213
00:16:36,172 --> 00:16:37,682
Were you joking?

214
00:16:38,256 --> 00:16:42,171
No, I'm not joking.

215
00:17:00,711 --> 00:17:05,850
In a year, I'll replace this
with a gold ring, I promise.

216
00:17:12,869 --> 00:17:17,940
Until the day I die, I'll protect
and respect Hui Na and her family,

217
00:17:18,174 --> 00:17:20,671
and I'll love her more than myself.

218
00:17:22,177 --> 00:17:24,109
I swear, Grandpa, Grandma.

219
00:17:38,136 --> 00:17:42,536
(Seo Min Ju)

220
00:17:46,735 --> 00:17:49,302
The call can't be connected.
You'll be connected to voicemail...

221
00:17:49,327 --> 00:17:50,570
(Kwon Hui Na)

222
00:18:14,422 --> 00:18:16,270
My legs are killing me.

223
00:18:17,070 --> 00:18:19,730
The new arrivals are no good this time.

224
00:18:26,132 --> 00:18:28,265
Order yours again.

225
00:18:37,282 --> 00:18:39,322
What is it?

226
00:18:47,545 --> 00:18:49,163
Is this the Han Gyu O you know, Mom?

227
00:18:49,689 --> 00:18:52,433
That's the Han Gyu O
you're desperately looking for, right?

228
00:18:52,873 --> 00:18:54,212
Well...

229
00:18:56,042 --> 00:18:59,606
Why do you have a picture of Gyu O?

230
00:18:59,631 --> 00:19:03,608
Han Gyu O is Kwon Hui Na's boyfriend!

231
00:19:19,082 --> 00:19:24,794
You'll leave once Mu Jin's a beggar,
won't you?

232
00:19:24,949 --> 00:19:27,342
You'll run off without even looking back.

233
00:19:27,372 --> 00:19:29,746
Hey! You...

234
00:19:30,461 --> 00:19:35,301
You think I can't spot parasites like you?

235
00:19:39,415 --> 00:19:45,991
Please, before I ruin Mu Jin for good.

236
00:19:46,688 --> 00:19:47,774
Hey!

237
00:19:48,688 --> 00:19:51,812
Hey, can't you just get lost?

238
00:19:51,837 --> 00:19:53,339
Please?

239
00:19:54,969 --> 00:20:00,813
Do you want to be some Cinderella
like your mom?

240
00:20:02,249 --> 00:20:04,798
Wake up, you little brat.

241
00:20:05,086 --> 00:20:10,101
Who am I? Me? I'm Hong Ok Seon. And you?

242
00:20:10,757 --> 00:20:15,709
Hey, you're a leech.

243
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:18,597
A cockroach!

244
00:20:43,473 --> 00:20:45,288
Like that's going to break anything.

245
00:20:49,502 --> 00:20:53,446
Kim Mu Jin is mine!

246
00:20:57,089 --> 00:20:59,184
Who's going to hear that?

247
00:21:04,089 --> 00:21:07,884
Kim Mu Jin belongs to Han Gyu Rim!

248
00:21:08,355 --> 00:21:10,840
I won't give him to anyone!

249
00:21:11,407 --> 00:21:15,314
This is real, right?
I'm not dreaming, am I?

250
00:21:19,396 --> 00:21:21,654
I love you, Kim Mu Jin!

251
00:21:22,774 --> 00:21:29,575
I love you to the moon and back,
more than the whole universe!

252
00:21:34,428 --> 00:21:38,100
This memory's going to keep me happy
for a thousand years.

253
00:21:38,125 --> 00:21:40,902
No, ten thousand years.

254
00:22:19,244 --> 00:22:22,938
Why am I sleeping here?

255
00:22:24,596 --> 00:22:26,529
My head...

256
00:22:27,336 --> 00:22:29,003
It smells like alcohol.

257
00:22:30,147 --> 00:22:34,309
My goodness. This was almost full.

258
00:22:35,303 --> 00:22:37,330
Did you drink all of this by yourself?

259
00:22:42,596 --> 00:22:46,133
Yeon Ju called me.
She asked if something happened to you.

260
00:22:46,769 --> 00:22:50,895
- She said you called and threatened her.
- Threatened her?

261
00:22:53,242 --> 00:22:55,424
That if she bragged about her husband
one more time,

262
00:22:55,449 --> 00:22:58,558
you'd tell everyone she had breast surgery
in the States in college.

263
00:22:59,371 --> 00:23:00,798
I said that?

264
00:23:01,003 --> 00:23:04,905
How much did you drink
to black out like that?

265
00:23:06,308 --> 00:23:08,554
Hold on.

266
00:23:14,591 --> 00:23:18,122
Hey, I really called Yeon Ju?
For 23 minutes?

267
00:23:20,584 --> 00:23:21,904
I must be crazy...

268
00:23:23,042 --> 00:23:26,567
Why? Did you cause trouble
with anyone else too?

269
00:23:28,141 --> 00:23:30,921
- I called Han Gyu Rim.
- What?

270
00:23:32,279 --> 00:23:34,312
What did you say to her?

271
00:23:35,536 --> 00:23:39,843
I blacked out.
How am I supposed to remember?

272
00:23:44,576 --> 00:23:46,443
Not here.

273
00:24:09,322 --> 00:24:12,608
- Good morning.
- Hey, good morning, Gyu Rim.

274
00:24:14,049 --> 00:24:18,614
This is a short video Gyu Min showed me.
Hold on a sec.

275
00:24:33,138 --> 00:24:34,558
Ta-da!

276
00:24:38,096 --> 00:24:41,726
Ta-da! This is Kim Mu Jin.

277
00:24:42,133 --> 00:24:45,200
Isn't he killing it?
Don't you just want to fall for him?

278
00:24:48,015 --> 00:24:51,313
- What are you doing?
- But you can't fall for him, everyone.

279
00:24:51,338 --> 00:24:54,272
Once you fall for Mu Jin,
there's no way out.

280
00:24:54,775 --> 00:24:57,037
Mu Jin is a black hole with no exit,

281
00:24:57,062 --> 00:25:03,317
and if you fall in, you might not survive,
so don't even look his way.

282
00:25:03,396 --> 00:25:06,633
And Mu Jin's already taken.

283
00:25:07,235 --> 00:25:12,322
He's got an absolutely amazing girlfriend
who's got it all!

284
00:25:13,269 --> 00:25:16,286
And that's me.

285
00:25:18,088 --> 00:25:21,931
I can't take it.
How are you so adorable, Han Gyu Rim?

286
00:25:26,569 --> 00:25:31,135
I wanted to make you laugh,
but just laugh at me instead.

287
00:25:32,182 --> 00:25:36,039
No. You gave me a good laugh
first thing in the morning.

288
00:25:36,342 --> 00:25:39,500
Once I hang up, I'm going to roll around
on the floor laughing.

289
00:25:39,675 --> 00:25:43,486
My dopamine's fully charged thanks to you.
Thanks, Gyu Rim.

290
00:25:44,342 --> 00:25:46,149
Let's not lose, Mu Jin.

291
00:25:46,882 --> 00:25:49,506
If you don't lose, you win.

292
00:25:50,882 --> 00:25:53,101
You're going to win, Mu Jin. I know it.

293
00:25:53,994 --> 00:25:56,234
You can do it, Kim Mu Jin. Hang in there.

294
00:25:57,162 --> 00:26:00,994
Thanks. That woke me right up.

295
00:26:15,522 --> 00:26:18,451
Hey, what happened to your eye?
Who did this?

296
00:26:18,756 --> 00:26:21,358
- I said, who did this to you?
- The family will hear you.

297
00:26:21,811 --> 00:26:23,136
Give me a name, now.

298
00:26:23,401 --> 00:26:25,136
I'll go and kill every last one of them.

299
00:26:25,136 --> 00:26:26,516
What school? What grade? What class?

300
00:26:28,375 --> 00:26:30,997
Why do you assume I got beat up?

301
00:26:32,390 --> 00:26:34,211
You obviously got hit.

302
00:26:34,361 --> 00:26:35,782
You think I can't tell by looking?

303
00:26:36,655 --> 00:26:40,074
Yeah, I got hit.
By some middle schoolers' baseball bat.

304
00:26:41,120 --> 00:26:42,129
What?

305
00:26:43,069 --> 00:26:46,088
Yesterday, I was taking rice cakes
to Su Nam's place for the opening.

306
00:26:46,441 --> 00:26:50,988
A middle schooler's bat flew into my eye,
and when I fell backward,

307
00:26:51,435 --> 00:26:53,812
I got scraped up all over.

308
00:26:54,637 --> 00:26:57,671
- Does that make any sense?
- Apparently, it does.

309
00:26:58,615 --> 00:27:01,922
All those middle schoolers came over
and even got down on their knees,

310
00:27:02,069 --> 00:27:04,462
and I met their parents
and went to the hospital.

311
00:27:05,168 --> 00:27:07,476
They said no broken bones, no injuries.

312
00:27:07,769 --> 00:27:11,676
Only my eye's swollen like a panda's.
It's just a bruise, see?

313
00:27:11,748 --> 00:27:12,862
What's the name of the hospital?

314
00:27:14,240 --> 00:27:16,421
You don't believe me?

315
00:27:17,656 --> 00:27:20,049
That's how little you trust me?

316
00:27:21,702 --> 00:27:24,471
I ran into Heung Sik at the hospital,

317
00:27:24,658 --> 00:27:26,924
so if you don't believe me,
call Heung Sik and ask him.

318
00:27:27,784 --> 00:27:29,704
What are you waiting for?
Go ahead and call.

319
00:27:30,640 --> 00:27:34,895
Why would those middle school punks
fling a baseball bat at your face?

320
00:27:35,569 --> 00:27:39,028
- With skills like that, why even play?
- I know, right?

321
00:27:39,689 --> 00:27:43,435
I'm going to go break up their team
today or tomorrow.

322
00:27:44,378 --> 00:27:47,184
What if it scars? What about school?

323
00:27:48,546 --> 00:27:52,621
I have to go. I've missed too much
because of modeling.

324
00:27:53,875 --> 00:27:55,970
I'll go get you some ointment
for your bruises and an eye patch.

325
00:28:00,968 --> 00:28:04,150
- You scared me!
- The real scare is over there.

326
00:28:04,709 --> 00:28:07,718
- Take a look at that punk's face.
- What?

327
00:28:14,970 --> 00:28:16,735
Did you just come back from a war?

328
00:28:18,909 --> 00:28:22,382
Your face is the only thing
you've got going for you.

329
00:28:22,407 --> 00:28:25,643
- What is this? Who did this to you?
- Just...

330
00:28:28,095 --> 00:28:31,324
- Why are you covering my mouth?
- In case you scream.

331
00:28:31,349 --> 00:28:33,258
Why? What is it?

332
00:28:34,708 --> 00:28:39,017
I wasn't going to tell the family
or you either,

333
00:28:39,912 --> 00:28:42,635
but you're a girl,
so you might be able to help.

334
00:28:45,154 --> 00:28:48,396
Gyu Yeong left her in-laws'.
She ran away from home.

335
00:28:48,421 --> 00:28:50,936
Hey! Han Gyu Yeong? Seriously?

336
00:28:57,842 --> 00:29:01,631
<i>The world is full of tasty food</i>

337
00:29:01,699 --> 00:29:05,749
<i>But to my taste, there's only you</i>

338
00:29:05,775 --> 00:29:09,452
<i>My heart races when I hear you bubble</i>

339
00:29:09,492 --> 00:29:13,555
<i>I gave my soul to this bright red broth</i>

340
00:29:14,399 --> 00:29:18,422
No "everyone for themselves" rule today.
I'll share my rice rolls. Have some.

341
00:29:19,636 --> 00:29:23,222
I'm good.
Ramen's 100 times better than rice rolls.

342
00:29:23,908 --> 00:29:26,619
There's tuna in the rice rolls too,
Grandpa.

343
00:29:27,149 --> 00:29:28,149
Tuna?

344
00:29:28,581 --> 00:29:31,813
That's okay.
I'll put tuna in my ramen, then.

345
00:29:32,895 --> 00:29:36,435
<i>I need nothing on my memorial table</i>

346
00:29:36,796 --> 00:29:39,942
<i>Just leave me some ramen</i>

347
00:29:40,029 --> 00:29:43,834
<i>Just leave me some tuna ramen</i>

348
00:29:49,083 --> 00:29:50,216
What was that?

349
00:29:50,656 --> 00:29:52,362
You said you wouldn't scream if I let go.

350
00:29:52,798 --> 00:29:54,422
How can I not scream?

351
00:29:54,822 --> 00:29:57,140
You're telling me you got beat up
like this because of Han Gyu Yeong.

352
00:29:57,642 --> 00:29:58,971
So I should've just let him drag her away?

353
00:29:58,996 --> 00:30:01,529
Yeah, you should have.
Why did you have to get involved?

354
00:30:01,569 --> 00:30:03,607
Han Gyu Yeong doesn't even treat us
like people,

355
00:30:03,608 --> 00:30:04,909
and you have no pride?

356
00:30:04,943 --> 00:30:06,816
Stop saying things you don't mean.

357
00:30:07,202 --> 00:30:09,062
If you'd been there,
you would've stepped in too.

358
00:30:09,347 --> 00:30:12,578
No, I wouldn't. No way.

359
00:30:13,198 --> 00:30:15,313
- It's pink eye.
- I'm coming in.

360
00:30:15,315 --> 00:30:16,542
Okay.

361
00:30:21,342 --> 00:30:22,558
What's wrong with Gyu Seo?

362
00:30:22,610 --> 00:30:23,677
- Pink eye!
- Pink eye.

363
00:30:25,135 --> 00:30:27,047
Pink eye? All of a sudden?

364
00:30:27,108 --> 00:30:29,042
What kind of pink eye? How did he get it?

365
00:30:29,148 --> 00:30:31,987
Don't. You can catch it just by looking.

366
00:30:32,036 --> 00:30:34,161
Look at me, Gyu Rim.
My eyes are already red, right?

367
00:30:34,595 --> 00:30:37,042
What pink eye spreads just by looking?

368
00:30:37,341 --> 00:30:39,828
- Han Gyu Seo, come here.
- No.

369
00:30:40,362 --> 00:30:42,758
My eyes are all gunky. I'm a mess.

370
00:30:42,985 --> 00:30:44,382
I don't want you to see me.

371
00:30:45,282 --> 00:30:46,539
Gyu Seo.

372
00:30:46,663 --> 00:30:49,877
Gyu Seo only wants you
to see his pretty face.

373
00:30:49,902 --> 00:30:53,482
His face is all he's got,
and his eyes are the GOAT.

374
00:30:53,507 --> 00:30:56,237
But he really doesn't want you
to see him, so don't look.

375
00:30:58,482 --> 00:31:00,609
Then why did you scream?

376
00:31:02,735 --> 00:31:05,829
Because I was so shocked
when I saw Gyu Seo's eye.

377
00:31:06,554 --> 00:31:10,226
It's so gross and nasty,
I can't even bear to look at it.

378
00:31:11,161 --> 00:31:12,727
I'd better get out of here
before I catch it.

379
00:31:16,421 --> 00:31:18,235
Then let's go to the eye doctor, Gyu Seo.

380
00:31:18,260 --> 00:31:20,302
Gyu O went to get
an eye patch and medicine.

381
00:31:21,022 --> 00:31:23,068
I've got Gyu O,
and I'm not a kid, Gyu Rim.

382
00:31:23,416 --> 00:31:25,576
In the old days,
I'd already have a son Gyeol's age.

383
00:31:27,034 --> 00:31:28,236
All right.

384
00:31:34,316 --> 00:31:39,138
What kind of pink eye is so bad
that you'd scream?

385
00:31:41,148 --> 00:31:43,993
- Why did you have Han Gyu Yeong?
- What?

386
00:31:44,455 --> 00:31:48,545
You should've just had Gyu Rim and Gyu O.
Why did you have Han Gyu Yeong?

387
00:31:50,424 --> 00:31:51,742
Did I give birth to her?

388
00:31:52,401 --> 00:31:56,262
Why have someone like Han Gyu Yeong
and make everyone worry for nothing?

389
00:31:57,548 --> 00:32:00,213
What about Gyu Yeong? Did you see her?

390
00:32:00,975 --> 00:32:02,824
Did Gyu Yeong pick on you again?

391
00:32:03,435 --> 00:32:06,356
I don't know. Anyway, karma's a beast.

392
00:32:11,991 --> 00:32:13,595
What is she talking about?

393
00:32:14,717 --> 00:32:18,802
Why bring up Gyu Yeong out of nowhere
while talking about Gyu Seo's pink eye?

394
00:32:19,526 --> 00:32:22,936
Do you know how hard
I'm trying to forget that name?

395
00:32:36,468 --> 00:32:39,263
You'll get indigestion, Gyu Min.

396
00:32:39,317 --> 00:32:41,357
Drink some water while you eat.

397
00:32:42,709 --> 00:32:44,192
Here you go.

398
00:32:47,142 --> 00:32:48,142
Thanks.

399
00:32:52,108 --> 00:32:55,079
Sorry, Gyu Rim. I'm the one
who said, "Everyone for themselves."

400
00:32:55,396 --> 00:32:59,079
I've been a little stressed out...

401
00:33:00,941 --> 00:33:04,611
Is there some connection between
Gyu Seo's pink eye and Gyu Yeong...

402
00:33:06,097 --> 00:33:08,362
No, there can't be.

403
00:33:12,628 --> 00:33:14,754
What did you mean by "karma's a beast?"

404
00:33:15,152 --> 00:33:18,715
What goes around comes around.

405
00:33:20,508 --> 00:33:22,269
Why did you suddenly say that?

406
00:33:22,749 --> 00:33:24,656
And bringing up Gyu Yeong out of nowhere?

407
00:33:27,736 --> 00:33:28,736
No reason.

408
00:33:28,839 --> 00:33:32,152
Last night, I dreamed
Han Gyu Yeong had pink eye.

409
00:33:32,177 --> 00:33:35,913
And then Gyu Seo came down with pink eye,
so it really got on my nerves.

410
00:33:37,314 --> 00:33:38,476
What time is it?

411
00:33:39,508 --> 00:33:42,603
I need to head to school. Bye, I'm off.

412
00:33:43,135 --> 00:33:45,300
- See you later.
- See you later.

413
00:33:57,836 --> 00:34:00,920
- Who are you calling?
- Gyu Yeong.

414
00:34:00,961 --> 00:34:04,024
The phone is off.
You'll be connected to voicemail.

415
00:34:04,049 --> 00:34:06,590
After the beep, you will be charged.

416
00:34:07,135 --> 00:34:08,674
It says her phone's off, right?

417
00:34:09,935 --> 00:34:13,496
She changed her phone
because she doesn't want our calls.

418
00:34:14,290 --> 00:34:15,589
Heartless girl.

419
00:34:17,522 --> 00:34:20,962
Gyu Yeong's really okay, right?

420
00:34:23,582 --> 00:34:25,829
This is jujube tea my mom brewed herself.

421
00:34:26,018 --> 00:34:27,791
She says it's a natural sedative.

422
00:34:30,780 --> 00:34:32,122
Have some whenever you feel like it.

423
00:34:36,422 --> 00:34:39,152
So what are you going to do
about that jerk Seong Uk?

424
00:34:40,635 --> 00:34:43,255
Shouldn't you have him locked up
for assault and attempted kidnapping?

425
00:34:44,774 --> 00:34:46,142
I'll think about it.

426
00:34:47,589 --> 00:34:49,695
Want me to go find him
and teach him a lesson?

427
00:34:51,815 --> 00:34:55,080
- You really want to go to jail?
- If I go, I go.

428
00:34:55,582 --> 00:34:58,038
Just stay out of it, please.

429
00:34:58,535 --> 00:35:00,328
I'd rather throw myself in the Han River.

430
00:35:08,115 --> 00:35:09,495
Did you call Gyu Seo?

431
00:35:11,155 --> 00:35:12,296
You tell him...

432
00:35:12,796 --> 00:35:14,681
that if he tells the family,
I won't let it slide.

433
00:35:15,015 --> 00:35:18,291
Not that. Tell him thanks for saving you.

434
00:35:19,795 --> 00:35:22,466
Tell him you've always been out
to get the twins,

435
00:35:22,585 --> 00:35:25,682
but he repaid that with kindness,
and you don't know how to thank him.

436
00:35:28,502 --> 00:35:30,225
Who asked him to save me?

437
00:35:33,185 --> 00:35:38,379
Hot blood doesn't run through your heart.

438
00:35:38,423 --> 00:35:40,249
Iced Americano does, right?

439
00:35:42,021 --> 00:35:43,647
Eat.

440
00:35:46,554 --> 00:35:51,372
Boys and girls over seven shouldn't mix.
What's with the closed door, you two?

441
00:35:51,861 --> 00:35:54,754
Even if boys and girls
attract like magnets,

442
00:35:55,628 --> 00:35:58,239
I'm not interested in a brat like this.

443
00:35:58,614 --> 00:36:01,440
Bring me a hundred truckloads of her.
I wouldn't even blink.

444
00:36:02,509 --> 00:36:04,369
Even if a girl's lost her mind,

445
00:36:04,390 --> 00:36:07,982
she can tell when people insult her
and say they don't like her.

446
00:36:09,376 --> 00:36:11,729
That vixen?

447
00:36:11,916 --> 00:36:14,852
A girl with not an ounce of compassion?

448
00:36:14,899 --> 00:36:17,862
I wouldn't want her,
not even a thousand truckloads of her.

449
00:36:18,445 --> 00:36:22,359
Mom, if you told me to marry
a woman like that,

450
00:36:23,127 --> 00:36:25,401
I'd shave my head and become a monk
right away.

451
00:36:28,936 --> 00:36:30,176
That rotten punk.

452
00:36:31,607 --> 00:36:34,366
He's not talking about you.

453
00:36:35,306 --> 00:36:40,039
There's a girl like that
in the third house in the rice cake alley,

454
00:36:40,109 --> 00:36:42,529
and he means her.

455
00:36:43,351 --> 00:36:48,910
I heard mackerel's good for the brain.
I stewed it with radish and aged kimchi,

456
00:36:48,935 --> 00:36:51,432
so let's go eat it while it's good.

457
00:36:54,655 --> 00:36:56,298
Are you upset?

458
00:36:58,888 --> 00:37:00,825
If you eat all your food like a good girl,

459
00:37:00,872 --> 00:37:05,413
I'll buy you ice cream later,

460
00:37:05,511 --> 00:37:08,649
and chicken too. What do you say?

461
00:37:09,015 --> 00:37:10,536
What do you say?

462
00:37:14,209 --> 00:37:16,270
It's best eaten hot...

463
00:37:16,295 --> 00:37:18,211
Nothing I can do.

464
00:37:18,777 --> 00:37:21,931
Okay. Eat whenever you feel like it, then.

465
00:37:23,836 --> 00:37:25,114
Hurry up and come.

466
00:37:28,822 --> 00:37:30,363
Gyu Yeong's sulking now.

467
00:37:31,308 --> 00:37:34,895
Heung Sik, she's pitiful enough as it is.

468
00:37:34,920 --> 00:37:37,348
Did you have to be so harsh to her?

469
00:37:51,042 --> 00:37:56,549
(Enjoy It Yourself, Go Under,
Get Lost, Kim Mu Jin!, Trash, Apologize)

470
00:37:56,550 --> 00:37:59,031
(Exposing Kim Mu Jin, the Corrupt Owner)

471
00:37:59,033 --> 00:38:01,193
(Shut It Down, Trash)

472
00:38:01,195 --> 00:38:03,508
(Go Under, Get Lost, Kim Mu Jin!)

473
00:38:11,065 --> 00:38:13,041
(Today's Special, Kim Mu Jin's Recycled
Food Waste, 150 Dollars Per Person)

474
00:38:13,066 --> 00:38:14,619
(Da Solo Restaurant Sells Trash for Money)

475
00:38:14,644 --> 00:38:16,217
(Recycled Leftovers, Fake Origin Labels)

476
00:38:16,574 --> 00:38:17,696
What...

477
00:38:19,998 --> 00:38:21,165
What is all this?

478
00:38:27,653 --> 00:38:30,942
Leave it. We have to preserve the scene!

479
00:38:34,862 --> 00:38:38,262
The CCTV will show everything,
so let's call the police first.

480
00:38:38,642 --> 00:38:40,815
Mu Jin, come on!

481
00:38:58,568 --> 00:39:01,488
You hungry? Want me to make you pasta?

482
00:39:03,634 --> 00:39:06,052
Did you go off and meditate or something?

483
00:39:09,936 --> 00:39:10,936
Should we fight?

484
00:39:11,542 --> 00:39:14,868
How do you think we should fight?

485
00:39:16,748 --> 00:39:21,036
But if I'm going to fight,
I'll fight properly to the end.

486
00:39:22,902 --> 00:39:26,908
Even if they cry and beg for mercy,
I won't let them off.

487
00:39:28,229 --> 00:39:31,157
And I won't give up halfway either.

488
00:39:31,969 --> 00:39:33,445
I won't let go until I die.

489
00:39:33,693 --> 00:39:35,506
Right. A Jindo dog.

490
00:39:36,041 --> 00:39:38,586
You've got that Jindo dog tenacity,
don't you?

491
00:39:39,662 --> 00:39:41,835
You're a total sweetheart,

492
00:39:42,176 --> 00:39:45,539
but once you snap, nobody can handle you.
That's Kim Mu Jin.

493
00:39:46,860 --> 00:39:49,814
Whoever you bite is done for.

494
00:39:52,331 --> 00:39:55,803
I'm hungry. I'll go make pasta.
Let's eat, then get to work.

495
00:40:06,295 --> 00:40:08,988
All our reservations have been canceled.

496
00:40:09,643 --> 00:40:12,825
No one's going to book anytime soon,

497
00:40:13,219 --> 00:40:15,773
and there won't be any walk-ins either,
will there?

498
00:40:17,869 --> 00:40:20,652
Everyone who passed the final interview
said they're not coming.

499
00:40:21,109 --> 00:40:22,109
Not even a phone call.

500
00:40:23,993 --> 00:40:26,521
They all turned it down by text.

501
00:40:31,483 --> 00:40:35,855
Without some dramatic turnaround,
how much longer can we hold out?

502
00:40:38,256 --> 00:40:41,782
Counting rent, loan interest,
ingredients, and so on,

503
00:40:43,860 --> 00:40:46,894
we've got 48 days at least, 63 at most.

504
00:40:50,768 --> 00:40:52,531
I saw a comment this morning...

505
00:40:52,936 --> 00:40:56,735
from someone who said
they found maggots in our food.

506
00:40:56,996 --> 00:41:01,387
I couldn't let that slide, so I got
every hacker I know to track them down,

507
00:41:01,412 --> 00:41:02,510
and guess who it was?

508
00:41:03,544 --> 00:41:04,829
A second grader.

509
00:41:05,016 --> 00:41:07,536
Who's never even been to our restaurant.

510
00:41:10,369 --> 00:41:12,561
The world's full of people picking fights.

511
00:41:13,289 --> 00:41:16,762
And stressed-out people angry
at this damn world are like,

512
00:41:16,787 --> 00:41:19,742
"Gotcha. Now you're dead."

513
00:41:20,396 --> 00:41:24,249
They've finally found a target,
and they're carpet-bombing us for fun.

514
00:41:26,482 --> 00:41:29,489
Sure, if we fought every one of them,
we could win.

515
00:41:29,570 --> 00:41:33,577
No, we're 100 percent innocent,
so we'd win every time in court.

516
00:41:33,602 --> 00:41:37,369
But what's the point of suing
and winning years later?

517
00:41:37,595 --> 00:41:38,969
By then, people will be thinking,

518
00:41:38,994 --> 00:41:42,967
"Was there ever a restaurant like that?"
They won't care at all.

519
00:41:49,025 --> 00:41:51,796
You said 48 days, right?
Sixty-three at most.

520
00:41:52,216 --> 00:41:55,736
And if I add some of my own money,
we can hold out a little longer.

521
00:41:55,762 --> 00:41:58,963
Don't you get it? The game's already over!

522
00:41:59,103 --> 00:42:00,709
Before you go totally broke...

523
00:42:02,729 --> 00:42:05,249
and end up even more of a wreck,
let's stop here.

524
00:42:06,133 --> 00:42:07,902
- No.
- Kim Mu Jin!

525
00:42:08,003 --> 00:42:09,329
You said we have 63 days.

526
00:42:10,082 --> 00:42:11,691
How do you know what I can do?

527
00:42:12,371 --> 00:42:14,922
I won't lose. Not even if it kills me.

528
00:42:15,829 --> 00:42:17,232
They said if you don't lose, you win.

529
00:42:18,431 --> 00:42:21,648
Gyu Rim said so too.
That I'd win in the end.

530
00:42:52,847 --> 00:42:57,018
When I was a clueless kid,
I scribbled on someone's wall,

531
00:42:57,562 --> 00:42:59,193
and I really regret it.

532
00:43:01,076 --> 00:43:05,338
If it's still there, I'd like to go
and apologize to them.

533
00:43:05,508 --> 00:43:08,431
Go find it. I'll go with you.

534
00:43:10,907 --> 00:43:14,724
Today, I'll clean everything up,
and tomorrow, I'll open for dinner.

535
00:43:15,286 --> 00:43:16,773
Even though there are no reservations.

536
00:43:17,762 --> 00:43:19,741
Maybe some customers will still come by.

537
00:43:20,156 --> 00:43:21,589
If not, so be it.

538
00:43:24,208 --> 00:43:28,008
I'll open up the kitchen
and the fridge too.

539
00:43:29,208 --> 00:43:32,669
If you want to see
how the food you eat gets made,

540
00:43:33,238 --> 00:43:34,955
come and see it for yourself.

541
00:43:35,676 --> 00:43:38,024
Sounds like you're going to war.

542
00:43:38,475 --> 00:43:42,439
Some people might think
it's just a cheap trick,

543
00:43:43,494 --> 00:43:46,493
but if you mean it, people can tell.
Why won't this come off?

544
00:43:47,949 --> 00:43:49,596
Just like you could tell with me.

545
00:43:55,214 --> 00:43:57,381
I've been thinking about something too.

546
00:43:59,840 --> 00:44:01,076
Will you hear me out?

547
00:44:03,268 --> 00:44:04,590
What is it?

548
00:44:25,182 --> 00:44:26,182
You...

549
00:44:27,825 --> 00:44:31,708
You think I can't spot parasites like you?

550
00:44:31,968 --> 00:44:33,341
Can't you just get lost?

551
00:44:33,700 --> 00:44:39,529
Do you want to be some Cinderella
like your mom?

552
00:44:40,443 --> 00:44:44,841
Wake up, you little brat.
You're a leech. A cockroach!

553
00:44:48,908 --> 00:44:51,647
I think I cursed at her or something?

554
00:44:54,128 --> 00:44:56,748
Even if I cursed,
I should've done it with some class.

555
00:44:56,773 --> 00:44:58,290
If I actually swore at her...

556
00:44:59,063 --> 00:45:01,365
She'll think I'm a terrible person.

557
00:45:02,557 --> 00:45:06,289
And I can't exactly call and ask her.

558
00:45:18,216 --> 00:45:21,060
- Hello.
- How's your stomach?

559
00:45:21,569 --> 00:45:24,008
You downed a bottle and a half
of soju yesterday.

560
00:45:25,756 --> 00:45:28,822
And on top of that,
I drank a whole bottle of liquor.

561
00:45:30,620 --> 00:45:33,009
So you mixed everything.

562
00:45:34,474 --> 00:45:36,609
Mixing drinks is bad for you.

563
00:45:37,109 --> 00:45:38,713
Should I bring you some medicine?

564
00:45:39,042 --> 00:45:41,510
No, I'm fine. I took some.

565
00:45:42,862 --> 00:45:46,000
Take a rockfish from the tank
at your sashimi restaurant.

566
00:45:46,025 --> 00:45:49,888
Make a clear fish soup with it,
and put in lots of bean sprouts.

567
00:45:50,782 --> 00:45:52,948
Bean sprouts are the best for hangovers.

568
00:45:52,973 --> 00:45:57,044
Speaking of bean sprouts,
that reminds me of someone.

569
00:45:58,631 --> 00:46:02,942
Bean sprouts.
Did you toss the bean sprouts?

570
00:46:03,763 --> 00:46:08,128
Did you toss them nice and good
with soy sauce and sesame oil?

571
00:46:12,222 --> 00:46:14,172
You always make me laugh.

572
00:46:14,280 --> 00:46:19,229
You're probably the only one in the world
who laughs at my dad jokes.

573
00:46:19,254 --> 00:46:21,987
That's why you and I are
such precious friends...

574
00:46:23,119 --> 00:46:24,735
You scared me. What is it?

575
00:46:24,908 --> 00:46:28,692
- Hey, what's wrong? What happened?
- Nothing.

576
00:46:31,215 --> 00:46:32,471
Welcome.

577
00:46:32,754 --> 00:46:36,162
A customer's here, so I'll call you later.

578
00:46:36,244 --> 00:46:38,876
Take care of yourself. Okay.

579
00:46:42,188 --> 00:46:45,456
Welcome. Looks like the owner
stepped out for a moment.

580
00:46:46,901 --> 00:46:50,217
I work here.

581
00:46:50,242 --> 00:46:52,809
I went to the restroom for a sec.

582
00:46:54,582 --> 00:46:57,312
You must be the new lady who started here.

583
00:46:58,702 --> 00:47:01,022
I'm the owner's dad.

584
00:47:07,675 --> 00:47:10,519
I look pretty young, don't I?

585
00:47:12,155 --> 00:47:16,555
Some people even think
I'm Gyu Rim's brother.

586
00:47:22,195 --> 00:47:27,028
But you look really familiar, ma'am.

587
00:47:28,095 --> 00:47:30,875
Have we met somewhere before?

588
00:47:31,562 --> 00:47:34,428
No. We've never met.

589
00:47:36,105 --> 00:47:37,855
I don't think so...

590
00:47:40,476 --> 00:47:44,796
I've definitely seen your face somewhere.

591
00:47:45,601 --> 00:47:48,977
That's because I have a friendly face.

592
00:47:50,355 --> 00:47:54,982
No, I wouldn't call it a friendly face.

593
00:47:55,242 --> 00:47:58,752
People say I'm pretty, though.

594
00:48:00,149 --> 00:48:04,635
Right. I didn't say you were ugly.

595
00:48:04,834 --> 00:48:09,121
But if I had to say, you're not my type.

596
00:48:14,660 --> 00:48:16,386
Excuse me...

597
00:48:17,433 --> 00:48:21,552
When my daughter comes in,

598
00:48:21,613 --> 00:48:26,602
please tell her that I bought her
red bean cakes to eat when she's hungry.

599
00:48:27,382 --> 00:48:29,668
You have some too, ma'am.

600
00:48:57,082 --> 00:49:02,452
Even if I got plastic surgery
and put a mole on my face,

601
00:49:02,726 --> 00:49:07,461
how can you not recognize the woman
who shared your bed and had your kids?

602
00:49:17,029 --> 00:49:18,521
Han Seok Jung.

603
00:49:19,395 --> 00:49:24,315
How are you still so handsome,
even at your age?

604
00:49:24,624 --> 00:49:26,235
It only makes me want you more.

605
00:49:30,524 --> 00:49:31,944
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

606
00:49:31,969 --> 00:49:34,790
Today, we'll start with prepping
for opening.

607
00:49:34,862 --> 00:49:37,422
You said you've never run a store before?

608
00:49:37,447 --> 00:49:43,384
No, but you explain it so well
that I feel really confident.

609
00:49:43,409 --> 00:49:44,620
Great.

610
00:49:44,645 --> 00:49:48,473
First, could you try showing customers
how to use the kiosk when they come in?

611
00:49:48,588 --> 00:49:50,461
- Sure.
- Just relax and give it a try.

612
00:49:50,538 --> 00:49:52,685
(Franchise Trainee)

613
00:49:52,795 --> 00:49:58,777
Ma'am, you can place your order
by tapping the kiosk like this.

614
00:49:59,606 --> 00:50:04,054
The more you order, the better the deal,
so please keep that in mind.

615
00:50:04,079 --> 00:50:05,658
You're doing great.

616
00:50:05,683 --> 00:50:07,713
Now let's try ingredient inspection.

617
00:50:07,738 --> 00:50:09,416
- Okay.
- This way.

618
00:50:18,709 --> 00:50:23,504
- This is the date we go by today.
- Okay.

619
00:50:23,529 --> 00:50:26,309
Check the fridge temperature twice a day.

620
00:50:26,468 --> 00:50:27,532
Got it.

621
00:50:27,557 --> 00:50:30,170
- I'll go check the other ingredients.
- Okay.

622
00:50:38,141 --> 00:50:42,187
You really seem like the owner.
Go, Ko Yun Hui!

623
00:50:42,508 --> 00:50:45,915
I'm officially becoming a regular.
I'll be eating here every day.

624
00:51:14,387 --> 00:51:18,216
Hello, sir. What brings you here?

625
00:51:18,250 --> 00:51:19,904
Congratulations.

626
00:51:20,640 --> 00:51:22,904
Thank you. You didn't have to...

627
00:51:22,929 --> 00:51:25,473
- Business going well?
- Yes, we're working hard.

628
00:51:25,498 --> 00:51:26,511
Good.

629
00:51:29,518 --> 00:51:30,607
Hello.

630
00:51:40,421 --> 00:51:41,483
Surprised?

631
00:51:42,931 --> 00:51:46,874
You're the youngest franchise owners
of all our stores nationwide,

632
00:51:47,177 --> 00:51:51,289
so I came by to thank you
and to see you for myself.

633
00:51:51,528 --> 00:51:54,642
Thank you. A customer just came in...

634
00:51:54,667 --> 00:51:56,100
- Go ahead.
- Take your time talking.

635
00:51:56,125 --> 00:51:57,619
- Okay.
- Welcome.

636
00:52:00,955 --> 00:52:03,915
I said we should have a meal together.
Why didn't you call?

637
00:52:04,076 --> 00:52:05,749
Did you think I was just being polite?

638
00:52:06,469 --> 00:52:10,778
I don't get why you keep asking
a guy like me to eat with you.

639
00:52:12,489 --> 00:52:13,528
Is that so?

640
00:52:15,018 --> 00:52:18,502
Still, wouldn't it be good
to know someone like me?

641
00:52:19,647 --> 00:52:24,676
In business, people around me think,
"Maybe I'll get some crumbs."

642
00:52:24,870 --> 00:52:26,796
There are a lot of them.

643
00:52:27,334 --> 00:52:29,127
I'm not interested in crumbs.

644
00:52:29,856 --> 00:52:32,589
Not even the kind on rice cakes.

645
00:52:38,728 --> 00:52:41,948
Genes are really something, aren't they?

646
00:52:42,681 --> 00:52:45,884
Once you dislike something,
gold and jewels won't sway you, right?

647
00:52:45,909 --> 00:52:50,931
You hate being a burden or owing anyone,
and you can't suck up to people.

648
00:52:52,674 --> 00:52:54,303
I'm talking about your mom.

649
00:52:55,235 --> 00:52:57,615
You take after her so much.

650
00:53:00,482 --> 00:53:02,308
What do you mean?

651
00:53:04,576 --> 00:53:07,236
I should've introduced myself sooner.

652
00:53:07,261 --> 00:53:10,687
I'm the one who lives with your mom.

653
00:53:17,002 --> 00:53:19,204
Your mom was exactly like that.

654
00:53:19,721 --> 00:53:24,965
When I first proposed,
she wouldn't give me the time of day.

655
00:53:25,802 --> 00:53:29,102
So I wondered if it was because
I was a widower with a kid,

656
00:53:29,127 --> 00:53:33,140
even though I'm a pretty successful
businessman in this industry.

657
00:53:34,669 --> 00:53:36,799
Anyway,
I chased her for a year and a half.

658
00:53:36,949 --> 00:53:41,707
I gave her so many bouquets in that time,
they'd fill a few flower shops.

659
00:53:42,401 --> 00:53:44,089
Just like you, Gyu O.

660
00:53:57,722 --> 00:54:02,436
I'm so glad my mom met
such a wonderful man.

661
00:54:04,109 --> 00:54:06,115
How do you know I'm a good man?

662
00:54:06,615 --> 00:54:09,140
Everyone who works
at this company knows...

663
00:54:09,855 --> 00:54:13,021
that you're a warm, wonderful man, sir.

664
00:54:15,282 --> 00:54:16,357
Thank you.

665
00:54:18,179 --> 00:54:21,120
Please, get up.

666
00:54:30,396 --> 00:54:32,076
So we're having that meal, right?

667
00:54:35,515 --> 00:54:36,541
Yes.

668
00:54:39,298 --> 00:54:43,335
How's your sister Han Gyu Yeong doing?

669
00:54:45,096 --> 00:54:47,334
We're not in touch.

670
00:54:48,949 --> 00:54:50,002
Is that so?

671
00:54:52,295 --> 00:54:54,062
Why ask about Gyu Yeong all of a sudden?

672
00:54:55,263 --> 00:54:56,563
Just...

673
00:54:56,894 --> 00:55:01,968
I thought we could all have a meal
with your sisters Gyu Rim and Gyu Yeong.

674
00:55:03,094 --> 00:55:05,988
All right. See you again.

675
00:55:12,315 --> 00:55:14,681
This is nice.

676
00:55:20,949 --> 00:55:25,064
- Am I coming here too often?
- Yes.

677
00:55:26,601 --> 00:55:29,474
What do you mean, too often?

678
00:55:29,499 --> 00:55:32,145
You came in the morning and at lunchtime.

679
00:55:32,456 --> 00:55:33,896
Were you counting?

680
00:55:33,921 --> 00:55:37,161
No, I wasn't counting. I simply remember.

681
00:55:44,274 --> 00:55:46,295
Is this some kind of hotel?

682
00:55:46,848 --> 00:55:48,945
Aren't you supposed to be working, ma'am?

683
00:55:49,815 --> 00:55:53,522
Why is everyone so obsessed
with how I do my job?

684
00:55:53,653 --> 00:55:58,948
I can see every customer coming from here,
so you don't need to worry.

685
00:56:02,715 --> 00:56:07,278
You've really got it made.

686
00:56:07,528 --> 00:56:11,433
How come you spend more time lying here
than at the side dish shop?

687
00:56:11,458 --> 00:56:15,462
Honestly! I can't even lie down in peace.

688
00:56:16,529 --> 00:56:20,057
Are you picking on a customer right now?

689
00:56:20,082 --> 00:56:23,101
- I'm not picking on you.
- I said I'm not picking on you.

690
00:56:23,125 --> 00:56:24,580
I'm not picking on you.

691
00:56:25,541 --> 00:56:27,344
One person at a time.

692
00:56:27,369 --> 00:56:29,928
Who asked for a three-dialect combo?

693
00:56:32,653 --> 00:56:36,729
Mom, what happened to that puppy
we adopted a few days ago?

694
00:56:36,754 --> 00:56:38,280
Did you leave her home alone?

695
00:56:38,774 --> 00:56:40,534
You adopted a puppy?

696
00:56:40,788 --> 00:56:44,849
Yes, she looks just like a fox.

697
00:56:45,929 --> 00:56:50,890
Someone came over and is playing with her,
so don't you worry.

698
00:56:50,915 --> 00:56:53,097
Someone? Who?

699
00:57:12,695 --> 00:57:15,561
I'm normal.
I'm playing dumb for a reason...

700
00:57:15,946 --> 00:57:21,621
I mean, I'm faking memory loss,
so just go.

701
00:57:29,283 --> 00:57:31,209
Is fraud your major or something?

702
00:57:31,682 --> 00:57:35,035
Faking memory loss and all,
conning even an old lady?

703
00:57:37,981 --> 00:57:40,095
Just try telling Su Nam.

704
00:57:40,120 --> 00:57:43,300
- You'll regret it.
- What are you going to do about it?

705
00:57:44,061 --> 00:57:46,639
- Hey.
- What?

706
00:57:47,442 --> 00:57:49,368
I said go.

707
00:57:49,393 --> 00:57:52,793
I'll pay you double for the session,
so just leave, you quack.

708
00:57:53,016 --> 00:57:56,662
Who do you think you are?
You're a criminal.

709
00:57:57,218 --> 00:57:58,424
Criminal?

710
00:57:59,401 --> 00:58:00,749
Who's a criminal?

711
00:58:00,815 --> 00:58:03,102
Did you see me commit a crime?

712
00:58:03,456 --> 00:58:05,416
I didn't see it, but I heard about it.

713
00:58:05,522 --> 00:58:08,928
If you wanted to con people,
do it yourself. Why drag my dad into it?

714
00:58:08,953 --> 00:58:11,603
Do you know what kind of situation
my dad's in because of you?

715
00:58:13,623 --> 00:58:14,863
Who are you?

716
00:58:16,941 --> 00:58:22,217
I'm the real daughter
of Mr. Jang Hun Tae, that's who.

717
00:58:31,129 --> 00:58:34,982
We'll serve one special dish,
a different one each day of the week.

718
00:58:38,669 --> 00:58:41,515
Dishes that were never on the menu.

719
00:58:55,982 --> 00:58:59,082
Dishes you can only get
at this restaurant.

720
00:59:28,889 --> 00:59:34,596
The one-of-a-kind dishes
you made just for me before, Mu Jin.

721
00:59:45,739 --> 00:59:48,585
How is it? Let me try too.

722
00:59:48,700 --> 00:59:50,517
Hold on a sec.

723
00:59:52,135 --> 00:59:53,411
It's pretty good.

724
01:00:46,916 --> 01:00:51,502
Taste it and see
if it's the flavor you loved,

725
01:00:52,302 --> 01:00:53,962
and be brutally honest.

726
01:01:46,341 --> 01:01:49,828
The customers will set the price
for the special dish.

727
01:01:50,375 --> 01:01:53,147
And if it's not good,
they don't have to pay.

728
01:02:05,948 --> 01:02:08,156
That was really delicious, Chef.

729
01:02:10,443 --> 01:02:12,506
Best meal I've ever had.

730
01:02:33,275 --> 01:02:35,059
(Han Gyu Rim)

731
01:02:43,482 --> 01:02:46,928
Hello, this is Han Gyu Rim.

732
01:02:47,849 --> 01:02:52,435
I was so flustered yesterday
that I couldn't give you an answer.

733
01:02:54,943 --> 01:02:59,297
I'll give you my answer now.

734
01:03:12,862 --> 01:03:16,495
I have a son named Gyeol.

735
01:03:18,648 --> 01:03:22,500
I love Mu Jin as much as I love Gyeol.

736
01:03:24,335 --> 01:03:29,195
If Gyeol is facing hardship,
I'll take the lead.

737
01:03:30,461 --> 01:03:35,703
If Gyeol is happy, I'll watch from behind.

738
01:03:40,479 --> 01:03:46,056
That's how I love Mu Jin.

739
01:03:50,135 --> 01:03:51,689
From now on,

740
01:03:52,577 --> 01:03:56,756
I will never be the first
to let go of Mu Jin's hand.

741
01:03:59,889 --> 01:04:01,277
I'm sorry.

742
01:05:00,080 --> 01:05:02,094
(Love on the Menu)

743
01:05:02,119 --> 01:05:04,348
My mom really wants to see Han Gyu O.

744
01:05:04,615 --> 01:05:06,237
Where is Han Gyu O?

745
01:05:06,239 --> 01:05:08,504
Please help me.
You said I'm your daughter too.

746
01:05:08,529 --> 01:05:10,122
Then act like a father.

747
01:05:10,162 --> 01:05:11,961
When kindness goes on too long,
people start to think it's their right.

748
01:05:11,986 --> 01:05:14,230
Anyway, why are you crying?
You're breaking my heart.

749
01:05:14,255 --> 01:05:16,335
Who do you think you are?

750
01:05:16,362 --> 01:05:17,916
Why are you making me feel pathetic too?

751
01:05:17,941 --> 01:05:20,430
No customers, Gyu Rim. Not a single one.

752
01:05:20,455 --> 01:05:23,687
Keep your promise
that you won't let go of my hand first.

753
01:05:23,712 --> 01:05:27,455
I hope Mu Jin goes under.

754
01:05:29,071 --> 01:05:30,871
Dramaday.me
